{
  "title": "iOS CI hand-rolls its xcodebuild invocation instead of using make \
targets",
  "description": ".github/workflows/ios.yml builds and tests with its own \
inline `xcodebuild test` command instead of `make ios-test` / `make \
ios-test-ui`, so build flags now live in three independently maintained places \
(the two Makefile targets and CI). The sign-simulator-test-builds fix had to \
patch all three, and future flag tweaks can silently drift between them — e.g. \
someone reintroducing CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO in one copy would resurrect the \
keychain/login failure there. Centralize on parameterized make targets that CI \
calls (destination/simulator id as a variable), keeping the invariant \
single-sourced, per the repo rule that everything goes through the Makefile.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "chore",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "ci",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-12T11:55:00-07:00",
